(a) the number of inoperative Employees' Provident Fund (EPF) accounts and the amount lying therein, year-wise and State/Union Territory-wise, from 2020-21 till date;
(b) the details of claims settled in respect of such accounts, year-wise, since then;
(c) whether Government has assessed the reasons for increase in the number of inoperative EPF accounts and if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the measures taken by Government to identify holders of inoperative EPF accounts, facilitate settlement of claims and reduce the number of inoperative EPF accounts and the quantum of unclaimed amount accumulations therein?

(a) whether Government is aware of the fact that a large number of deaths resulting from road accidents can be prevented if timely medical treatment is provided;
(b) if so, the number of road accident victims in the country benefited from the Prime Minister-Road Accident Victims' Hospitalisation and Assured Treatment (PM RAHAT) scheme so far and the State-wise/Union Territory-wise details thereof;
(c) the amount paid to the hospitals under the said scheme till date and the details of pending demands; and
(d) the steps being taken by Government to ensure the effective implementation of the scheme, registration of more and more hospitals and ensuring treatment 'within one hour of accident'?

(a) whether Government is aware of the increasing incidents of cyber fraudsters emptying bank accounts by sending fake e-challans;
(b) the number of such cases registered in the last two years, the amount that has been scammed, the number of cases resolved and the detail of action taken against the culprits;
(c) the special training and resources being provided by Government to State police and cyber cells for the investigation of such cybercrimes; and
(d) whether Government is operating any time-bound mechanism to assist victims of such cyber frauds in swift recovery of funds, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the year in which the annual allocation amount per Member under MPLADS was last revised;
(b) whether Government has conducted any assessment of the adequacy of the current amount of ?5 crore per Member; 
(c) whether Government has received any representations from Members regarding an increase in the annual allocation under the Members of Parliament Local Area Development Scheme (MPLADS); 
(d) if so, the details thereof; 
(e) whether any proposal to increase the said amount is currently under consideration by Government; and 
(f) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the number of States and Urban Local Bodies presently included under the National Urban Digital Mission (NUDM) and the status thereof;
(b) the measures taken under the mission to ensure the security of citizens' personal data, cybersecurity and privacy;
(c) whether Government has conducted any assessment regarding the extent of improvement brought in the quality of citizen services, transparency and the grievance redressal system due to this mission, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the special measures taken under the mission to extend the benefits of digital services to women, senior citizens, persons with disabilities and economically weaker sections?

(a) whether Government is undertaking the comprehensive redevelopment of railway stations, including passenger amenities and freight terminals in Rajasthan;
(b) if so, the details thereof, including the budget allocation for the redevelopment; and
(c) the details of the upgradation works undertaken under the Amrit Bharat Station Scheme (ABSS) in Rajasthan and the financial support provided therefor, city-wise?

(a) whether it is a fact that there has been a significant decline in the number of foreign tourists visiting Rajasthan, resulting in a substantial drop in hotel bookings;  
(b) if so, the details thereof and the reasons therefor;  
(c) whether it is also a fact that a decline has been recorded in the revenue generated from domestic tourists at specific locations such as Amer Fort and Albert Hall; and  
(d) the steps Government is considering to take in order to promote the arrival of foreign and domestic tourists in Rajasthan this year?

(a) the year-wise and source-wise share of renewable energy in the country’s total energy supply mix from 2021-22 till date;
(b) whether renewable energy’s share in the country’s total primary energy supply remains low despite growth in installed capacity, if so, the reasons thereof;
(c) what measures Government is taking to bridge this gap; and
(d) the year-wise and source-wise share of renewable energy in the country’s electricity generation from 2021-22 till date, along with the quantum of electricity generated from each renewable source?

(a) whether it is a fact that household budgets are under severe strain due to the sharp increase in prices of essential commodities such as pulses, vegetables, edible oils and flour;
(b) if so, the percentage increase in the prices of essential commodities during the last one year and the reasons therefor; and
(c) whether Government is considering to take any measures to control the rising prices, as steep price hikes have forced several families to reduce or eliminate essential food items from their diet?

(a) whether it is a fact that an increasing number of motorists are opting for high-octane petrol due to concerns that E20 is affecting fuel mileage and engine performance as E20 petrol has now become the default fuel across the country;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether prices of premium petrol have increased significantly during the last one year, if so, the details of increase in its prices during the last 12 months; and
(d) quantity of ethanol being procured every month by the petroleum companies, along with the details thereof, including the names of the purchasing companies and the suppliers?

(a) whether it is a fact that the Supreme Court of India has expressed concern over exorbitant airfares, describing them as exploitative for passengers and has urged Government to ensure their rationalisation at the earliest;
(b) if so, the steps taken by Government in compliance with the directions and observations of the Supreme Court;
(c) whether it is also a fact that airlines substantially increase airfares during festivals such as Diwali, Christmas and other peak travel seasons without any justifiable reason; and
(d) if so, the measures proposed to be taken by Government to regulate and keep airfares at reasonable levels during festivals and peak travel seasons?

(a) whether there has been a 28.7 per cent decline in India's textile and apparel exports to the USA market, while Vietnam's exports have increased by 5 per cent;
(b) if so, the steps being taken by Government to prevent this loss of market share and the associated impact on employment;
(c) whether Government has been able to secure better tariff/trade deals for India compared to countries like Vietnam, if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor; and
(d) whether Government has a concrete, time-bound plan to bring orders back from countries like Vietnam and Bangladesh?

(a) whether it is a fact that advertisements and other material relating to sexual exploitation of children are abundantly available on electronic platforms;
(b) if so, the details thereof and the action taken by Government to immediately deactivate such material; and
(c) Government's policy with regard to advertisements displayed on Instagram and the reasons for displaying such material on platforms accessible in India?

(a) the major reasons for delay in implementation of e-Courts Mission Mode Project in Rajasthan;
(b) whether Government has the district-wise details of the progress achieved so far in the State as compared to the targets prescribed and If so, the details thereof;
(c) the number of district and subordinate courts in the State in which facilities such as e-Filing, virtual hearings, digital records management and video conferencing are fully operational; and
(d) whether Government has prescribed any revised time-frame for completion of pending works under e-Courts Mission Mode Project there and if so, the likely date of completion of the Project?

(a) the year-wise average real wages of workers in the rural and urban areas since 2021, including the categories of regular salaried employees, casual labourers and self-employed workers;
(b) whether Government has undertaken any assessment of the impact of stagnant real wages on domestic consumption and the standard of living in the country and if so, the details thereof; and
(c) the measures taken or proposed by Government to improve wage growth, quality of employment and income security for workers in both the organised and unorganised sectors?

(a) whether it is a fact that, under 'Operation Checkmate', 52 persons, including 36 semi-truck drivers, were recently arrested by the United States Border Patrol, of whom 30 were Indian nationals;
(b) whether Government has obtained, from the United States authorities, the particulars of these 30 Indian nationals, including their home States/districts and details of their families;
(c) if so, the steps being taken for their rehabilitation/reintegration after deportation;
(d) whether the Indian Embassy Consulate was informed prior to these arrests; and
(e) the action taken to provide legal assistance and consular access to these Indian nationals?

(a) district-wise number of children identified and supported under PM-CARES for children scheme in Rajasthan since the launch of the said scheme;
(b) the details of the benefits provided to such children, including financial assistance, educational support, health insurance and residential care; and
(c) whether any information about shortcomings or delays have been reported regarding the identification, documentation, or delivery of benefits to eligible children in the State, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the details of the perpetrators involved in Input Tax Credit fraud cases during the last three years, State-wise and sector-wise;
(b) the stringent measures being taken by Government to deal with cases of Input Tax Credit fraud during the said period; 
(c) the number of fake GST registrations obtained through the misuse of forged PAN cards and Aadhaar cards; and
(d) the number of individuals arrested in such cases over the past three years and the number of masterminds still absconding?

(a) the increase or decrease in pending payments of MSMEs over the last three years;
(b) the number of complaints registered on the MSME solution portal with Government so far;
(c) whether it is a fact that several Government departments and Public Sector Undertakings (PSUs) themselves are not making timely payments to MSMEs, if so, the action taken by Government against such departments/PSUs; and
(d) the number of MSMEs closed or came under financial distress due to delayed payments, the State-wise details thereof?

(a) the State-wise detail of complaints received regarding electric poles falling or high-tension wires snapping during the past two years;
(b) the State-wise detail of the number of human and animal deaths caused by such incidents;
(c) whether such incidents are a result of negligence on the part of officials, if so, the detail of actions taken against the concerned officials; and
(d) the strict steps taken by Government for the regular inspection of electricity lines in order to prevent such accidents in the future?

(a) whether Government has implemented the National Handicraft Development Programme (NHDP) to facilitate the establishment of Urban Haats in major cities with a view to provide direct marketing facilities to artisans/weavers;
(b) if so, the number of Urban Haats presently operational in the country, including the State of Rajasthan; and 
(c) whether Government has received any proposals from the Government of Rajasthan for the establishment of new Urban Haats, if so, the details and present status thereof?

(a) total budget allocated for the ongoing Information Technology (IT) training programmes in the country in the current financial year; 
(b) number of youth trained under these IT training programmes during the last three years and the number of those who secured employment, along with details thereof;
(c) whether the number of IT training centres in rural and backward areas is inadequate, if so, the efforts being made by Government to address the shortfall; and
(d) whether Government has made any special provisions for providing IT training to youth belonging to the Scheduled Castes (SCs), Scheduled Tribes (STs) and Other Backward Classes (OBCs)?

(a) the specific measures being taken by Government to increase the value addition to telecommunication equipments in the country;  
(b) the comparative details of benefits extended to Indian and global companies;   
(c) the number of companies which have achieved their investment and production targets; and  
(d) the details of Government’s strategy to make India a global telecommunication equipment manufacturing hub in future?

(a) whether cases of corruption have been reported in several sports federations, depriving deserving coaches, players and other staff of proper opportunities and if so, the action taken against the officials involved;
(b) the action taken by Government on reports of administrative lapses and misuse of funds in sports federations across the country; and
(c) the policy of Government to address concerns regarding the autonomy of National Olympic Committee and National Sports Federations?

(a) the details of progress made, so far, by Government to bring unorganized sector workers under the ambit of social security schemes;
(b) the percentage of workforce presently under social security coverage in the country, State-wise; and
(c) the details of action plan of Government for extending social security coverage to women, domestic workers along with gig and platform workers?

(a) whether there is an urgent need for the development of commercially viable and professionally managed retirement housing projects due to the steadily ageing population and the growing trend of nuclear families;
(b) if so, the number of such projects under implementation, State-wise; and 
(c) the details of the facilities provided to senior citizens in these housing projects?

(a) whether Government proposes to increase the speed limits for different categories of vehicles on roads, particularly expressways;
(b) if so, the details thereof; 
(c) whether it is also a fact that there should be a uniform maximum speed limit across all cities in order to avoid confusion over speed limits; and 
(d) if so, the steps being taken by Government in this regard?

bs

(a) whether Government is implementing the Waterways development project under National Waterway-1 (NW-1) on the River Ganga;
(b) if so, the present status of progress of the project and the expenditure incurred thereon so far;
(c) the estimated annual cargo handling capacity expected to be achieved through this project;
(d) whether the details of the multi-modal terminals and other infrastructure facilities developed under this project are available; and
(e) whether Government has conducted any study regarding employment generation and the reduction in cargo transportation costs associated with this project?

(a) the State-wise details of gas or chemical leakage incidents in the country during the last five years;
(b) whether Government has taken any punitive action against the industrial units responsible for these accidents, if so, the details thereof; and
(c) whether Government is considering to establish a special monitoring mechanism in collaboration with the States to ensure compliance with safety standards in industrial areas, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the details of plan to provide training in new technological areas such as drones, air traffic management and aviation cyber security;
(b) whether Government has collaborated with any international aviation institution or foreign university for skill development programmes;
(c) the special initiatives being undertaken to provide training and employment to women and other minority groups in the aviation sector; and
(d) Government's estimate of the human resource requirement in the aviation sector over the next five-ten years and the skill development programmes being implemented to meet it?

(a) the number of objections received from stakeholders during the public consultation period in respect of draft Central Rules relating to the new Labour Codes;
(b) whether Government has prepared a subject-wise compilation of the comments received and placed the same in the public domain;
(c) whether any changes have been made in the final rules based on these representations and if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the State/Union Territory-wise status of framing and notification of respective State Rules under each Code and the steps taken by Government to ensure harmonization and timely implementation thereof?

(a) whether Government has undertaken any assessment to evaluate the impact of Know India Programme (KIP) in strengthening the cultural, emotional, and developmental engagement of overseas Indian youth with India;
(b) the number of participants who have benefited from the programme during the last five years, country-wise; and
(c) whether Government proposes to expand the programme in terms of participant capacity, number of editions conducted annually or coverage of countries in view of the growing global Indian diaspora and if so, the details thereof?

(a) the number of youths who secured employment in foreign countries under Government schemes during the last three years;
(b) the steps being taken by Government to ensure that youth working in foreign countries receive minimum wages, social security and labour rights;
(c) whether Government plans to launch any new scheme to provide skill training to the youth in accordance with the demands from foreign countries, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) whether any special scheme is proposed for the rehabilitation and re-employment of youth who have returned from foreign countries, if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether one of the major reasons for the increasing traffic problem in major cities of the country is the registration of vehicles on the basis of false affidavits regarding the availability of valid parking and if so, the steps taken by Government in this regard;
(b) whether most of the four-wheeler buyers avail loans from banks, non-Government financial institutions or finance companies;
(c) whether banks obtain an affidavit regarding the availability of valid parking from vehicle buyers at the time of sanctioning loans and if not, the reasons therefor; and
(d) whether Government proposes to issue any guideline or issue instructions to financial institutions in this regard?

(a) whether Government has evaluated the impact of the currently rising prices of gas cylinders and if so, the key findings thereof;
(b) whether Government has considered taking any measures to curb the rise in prices or to provide relief to common citizens;
(c) whether Government is considering to stabilise the prices of domestic LPG cylinders or making the subsidy scheme more effective, so that the poor and the middle class can benefit directly; and
(d) the strategy of Government to prevent such price hikes in the future?

(a) the Budget allocation and actual expenditure of the Geological Survey of India (GSI) during the last five financial years, year-wise;
(b) whether Government has taken cognizance of observations of the Department-related Parliamentary Standing Committee regarding financial constraints in GSI;
(c) whether any projects relating to critical and strategic minerals have been delayed or deferred due to financial or manpower constraints; and
(d) the steps taken or proposed to augment financial allocation and technical capacity of GSI to meet the increased exploration requirements, particularly for critical minerals?

