(a) the details of the quantity and value of bitumen imported into the country since 2015-16, along with the country-wise sources of such imports year-wise;
(b) the details of domestic production and total domestic consumption of bitumen during the same period and the percentage share of imports in total domestic consumption year-wise; and
(c) whether Government has assessed the adequacy of domestic bitumen production capacity in meeting the demand arising from national highway and infrastructure development programmes and if so, the details thereof?

(a) the districts in Rajasthan that have been selected by Government under the One District One Product (ODOP) scheme as part of the Atmanirbhar Bharat initiative, along with the products identified for each district;
(b) whether traditional products such as Jaipur Blue Pottery, Jodhpur Furniture and Bhilwara Textile Industry are included under this scheme, if so, the specific steps taken to promote them; and
(c) the number of artisans, micro and small entrepreneurs in Rajasthan who have received direct or indirect employment through this scheme?

(a) whether Government maintains data on industrial production growth rates and, if so, the details thereof, State-wise;
(b) whether the decline in the industrial production growth rate has adversely affected employment generation in the country;
(c) the major reasons for the fluctuations observed in industrial production growth rates during the last three years; and
(d) whether Government is considering to introduce any new policy to accelerate industrial production growth?

SR

(a) whether Government is aware that elderly pensioners are facing persistent difficulties with biometric authentication for digital life certificates, particularly due to fingerprint failures;
(b) if so, the manner in which Government is addressing this issue;
(c) whether Government has done any assessment of pensioners who have been unable to obtain digital life certificates, so far; and
(d) whether any special arrangements have been made to address the practical difficulties faced by senior citizens, especially pensioners above 80 years of age, in using this system?

(a) the aims and objectives of conferring the National Teachers’ Award on teachers;
(b) the criteria adopted for the selection of teachers for the National Teachers’ Awards conferred on 5th September each year;
(c) the number of teachers honoured with the National Teachers’ Award in the current year and the funds allocated and utilized for this purpose during each of the last three years and the current year;
(d) whether Government has any proposal to grant out-of-turn promotion to award-winning teachers, if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the facilities or incentives that are being provided to the award-winning teachers?

